WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.234 --> 00:00:01.660
(lively guitar music)

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.480
- I set the record for the lowest limbo

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.610
of 8.5 inches in 2010.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:06.760
I'm very proud of that.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.340
My name is Shemika Campbell,

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.513
and I am a world class limbo dancer.

00:00:17.957 --> 00:00:18.790
(steel drum music)

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.470
I'm originally from Trinidad and Tobago,

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.800
which is also where
limbo dance originated.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.850
It was a dance at wakes that symbolized

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.410
entering from one life to another.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:29.653
Now today, it's literally everywhere.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.340
I got into the art of
limbo at the age of 14.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.120
My grandmother was a limbo dancer,

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.117
my mother was a limbo dancer

00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:39.710
and it's only right
that I'm a limbo dancer.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.170
I had to carry on that legacy,

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.710
not only for my family,

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.802
but also for my culture, as well.

00:00:44.802 --> 00:00:45.635
(bright music)

00:00:45.635 --> 00:00:47.470
Physically, I am very flexible.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:49.650
I do my daily stretches.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.460
I can't really feel normal stretches,

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.910
so I have to like create my own,

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.470
to where I really feel
the stretch in my legs.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.503
I get a little crazy sometimes, for sure.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:03.055
- Ladies and gentlemen, the
limbo queen, Shemika Campbell.

00:01:03.055 --> 00:01:03.888
(cheering)

00:01:03.888 --> 00:01:06.490
- [Shemika] In order to
make it under 8.5 inches,

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:08.590
I have to hold my breath in order

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.823
to contort my body to
make it under the bar.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.610
At the same time I have to think

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:18.230
about my arms, I have to
think about my positioning.

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:19.950
I move side to side just to show

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.370
that I'm still suspended.

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:24.150
I start to move actually
physically under the bar

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.320
and that's pretty much when I'm able

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.920
to let the air out.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.540
And that's when I will get up.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:31.170
It's very very very hard to do.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.950
The pain that I feel during practicing

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.910
and pushing myself that comes with it,

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:36.950
that's one of the things

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:38.440
that really drew me to limbo.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.640
It was something that
I couldn't do easily.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.070
I love the challenge.

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:44.974
Me making it under this
bar perfectly every time,

00:01:44.974 --> 00:01:47.133
it means the absolute world.

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.383
(cheering)

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.470
I pretty much limbo any and everywhere.

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.390
I've been on “America's Got Talent” twice.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:58.990
I've been on “The Ellen Degeneres show.”

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:02.010
I've been on “The Late Late
Show with James Corden.”

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.850
When I see peoples' reactions

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:05.630
and how appreciative they are

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:08.723
of my ability to do this is just amazing.

00:02:09.704 --> 00:02:10.925
Alright.

00:02:10.925 --> 00:02:11.758
Put it there, put it there.

00:02:11.758 --> 00:02:12.810
- I really do appreciate
you representing the city.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.270
- I absolutely love limbo.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.010
I love everything about it.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:19.460
People think that limbo is just for fun.

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.340
For Trinidadians like myself,

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.180
it's really a big part of our culture.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.720
I feel like that's where my job comes in,

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.220
to really show you this is more

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.298
than just a fun little activity.

00:02:28.298 --> 00:02:29.294
- [Man] Whoa.

00:02:29.294 --> 00:02:32.627
(clapping and cheering)

